In a research note with GF Securities today, Pu said the iPhone Air 2 will have the following five new features compared to the current model:<ul><li>The addition of <strong>a second 48-megapixel rear camera</strong> — an Ultra Wide lens to complement the existing Fusion lens.</li><br/>
  <li>A slightly <strong>smaller Dynamic Island</strong>.</li><br/>
<li>A faster and more power-efficient <strong>A20 Pro chip</strong> manufactured with TSMC's advanced 2nm process. The current iPhone Air has a 3nm A19 Pro chip.</li><br/>
  <li>Apple's second-generation <strong>N2 chip</strong> for wireless networking. In the existing iPhone Air, the N1 chip is an Apple-designed wireless networking chip that enables Wi-Fi 7, Bluetooth 6, and Thread. The chip also improves the overall performance and reliability of features like AirDrop and Personal Hotspot.</li><br/>
  <li>Apple's second-generation <strong>C2 chip</strong> for 5G. Apple says the current C1X chip is already the most power-efficient modem in an iPhone ever.</li></ul>He expects the next iPhone Air to stick with a 6.5-inch display, 12GB of RAM, and an 18-megapixel Center Stage front camera.<br/>
